📘 Experiment Title

Implementation of Linear Regression

🎯 Aim

To implement Linear Regression and predict the marks for a given input using the trained model.

📖 Theory

Linear Regression is a supervised machine learning algorithm used to predict a continuous value based on input features.

It assumes a linear relationship between input (X) and output (Y).

The equation of a straight line is:

𝑦=𝑏0+𝑏1𝑥

Where:
y = Predicted output (Marks)
x = Input (e.g., study hours)
b0= Intercept
b1= Slope

🔢 Algorithm Steps
Import required libraries
Prepare dataset (input and output values)
Create Linear Regression model
Train the model using data
Predict output for new input
Plot graph of actual vs predicted values


💻 Program
from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression
import numpy as np
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
X = np.array([1,2,3,4,5]).reshape(-1,1)
y = np.array([35,40,50,60,65])
model = LinearRegression()
model.fit(X, y)
pred = model.predict([[6]])
print("Predicted Marks:", pred)
plt.scatter(X, y)
plt.plot(X, model.predict(X))
plt.xlabel("Input")
plt.ylabel("Marks")
plt.title("Linear Regression")
plt.show()

